00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, MARCH 1, 2006\r\rMayor Groveman called the meeting to order at 7:45 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Groveman, Mayor pro Tem Washburn, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Lysik, Mink, Parker, Peirce, Steller, Tamuri.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Robert Yalda.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Washburn to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\r Councilmember Bozajian expressed his appreciation for the participants of the de Anza event. Mayor pro Tem Washburn announced the upcoming Citywide Creek Clean-up events on March 18, and March 26, 2006.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT \r\r June Woodmansee, Calabasas, requested the City Council�s assistance in acquiring high speed internet access in Calabasas Village Mobile Estates.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the February 15, 2006 City Council meeting. \r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2006-215, amending Chapters 2.36, 2.37, 2.38, 2.40 and 2.43 of the Calabasas Municipal Code, regarding citizenship requirements for City Commissions. \r\r Adoption of Ordinance Nos. 2006-219, 2006-220, 2006-221, and 2006-222, which propose to amend various chapters of Title 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code. \r\r Recommendation to adopt Resolution No. 2006-1010, requesting Los Angeles County to accept transfer of storm drain improvements for M.T.D. 1622, for future maintenance and operation, New Millennium Homes Tract 35596. \r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1011, accepting the Los Angeles County Community Development Commission�s (CDC) offer to exchange the City of Calabasas� unallocated Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) funds totaling $85,000 at a rate of $0.65 of general fund revenue for every CDBG dollar, for a total of $55,250. \r\r \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Recommendation to approve the appointment of Matthew Heller by Councilmember Washburn to the Parks, Recreation and Education Commission, term ending March 31, 2007. \r\r Recommendation to approve the Art in Public Places Advisory Committee. \r\r Approval of permanent part-time Building Inspector position. \r\rMayor pro Tem Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian to approve Items #1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 and 8 with Mayor Groveman ABSTENTION on Item #4. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1012, approving a mitigated negative declaration; adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1013, approving GPA-004-003, PM-004-001, CUP-004-006, VAR-004-005 and OTP-005-009; and motion to waive further reading and introduction of Ordinance No. 2006-223, approving ZCH-004-005 for the subdivision of one parcel into two parcels, rough grading of one pad and driveway on one resulting parcel, and development of one single-family home including a pool/spa, horse stable/corral area, septic system, driveway, and retaining walls and dedication of 8.7 acres of permanent open space on the second resulting property located at 24135 Mulholland Highway (APN�s: 4455-006-012, -013). \r\rCouncilmember Wolfson recused himself due to the proximity of his residence to the project and left the room.\r\rMayor Groveman opened the public hearing.\r\rAndy Howard, Applicant, stated that he will not be in town on April 5, 2006 for the continued public hearing, however he has a consultant who would be available to attend if necessary.\r\rMayor Groveman closed the public hearing.\r\rMayor pro Tem Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to continue the public hearing to April 5, 2006. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Wolfson recused himself from the public hearing.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS\r\r Appointment of the Alternate to the Planning Commission. \rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson to appoint Rick Schumacher as the Alternate to the Planning Commission. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Discussion regarding the future direction of the Agoura Hills/Calabasas Community Center. \r\rJeff Rubin, Director of Community Services, provided the staff report.\r\rNo Action Taken.\r\r Recommendation to accept final design plans and specification for the A.E. Wright Pedestrian Footbridge project, and to direct staff to solicit bids for construction. \r\rMayor pro Tem Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian to approve the staff�s recommendation.\r\r Discussion regarding the procedure for issuance of a legislative subpoena. \r\rThe City Council directed the City Attorney to send a letter to the Regional Postmaster, compelling him to attend a special meeting on March 22, 2006 with the City Council to investigate postal problems with further direction to invite Congressman Waxman�s and U.S. Senator�s offices to also attend the meeting.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of February 3, 2006 to February 17, 2006. \r\r No Action Taken.\r\r\r\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r Mayor pro Tem Washburn provided brief reports on the Civic Center Task Force and the Mountains Restoration Trust.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles stated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\rThe City Council requested a report on activities at Southern California Association of Governments and Santa Monica Bay Restoration Commission on a future agenda.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:15 p.m. in memory of Carl Gibbs.\r\r\r\r\r_____________________________